{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1417506-denizen-scions-a-question","id":1417506,"title":"Denizen Scions: A Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-09T20:05:09-07:00","id":1417506,"title":"Denizen Scions: A Question","content":"Suppose a Denizen becomes a Scion. Suppose this Denizen's Supernatural Origin Path is exclusive to a single culture. Is the Denizen capable of becoming Scion to any god, or must they be bound to one from the very culture that they themselves come from?<br /> To put it another way, suppose the Supernatural Origin Path reads \u00c1os Sidhe Captive. Can they become the Scion of say, Amaterasu, or are they limited to the Irish deities?<br /> If they are not so limited, what might the consequences of such a decision be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T20:12:35-07:00","id":1417508,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s nothing that limits a Denizen to any single pantheon for Scionhood really, if you want to play say a Kitsune whose the child of Mithra of the Yazata go right ahead. The consequences can be decided by the table, based on what is most dramatic for the story, honestly there aren\u2019t any general consequences because while possible such characters are by definition unusual even by the standards of Scion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T20:26:25-07:00","id":1417509,"title":"","content":"Incarnate Scions will be of a suitable heritage. In this case, it <i>might</i> be argued that you won't find a reincarnation of Amateratsu that is an \u00c1os Sidhe \u2014 though stranger things have happened. <br /> <br /> Made Scions (I forget the official name) can be whatever their Maker can make. So, similar to the Incarnate Scions, you're only as likely to be made as an \u00c1os Sidhe Scion of Amateratsu as Amateratsu is to make an \u00c1os Sidhe. <br /> <br /> Born Scions will have one parent from the Pantheon; but the other parent can be anything that a god can procreate with. If Amateratsu sleeps with an \u00c1os Sidhe and a child is conceived, that child will be a Scion of Amateratsu. <br /> <br /> Chosen Scions can be anything; they merely have to catch the god's eye enough for him and/or her to invest in them. We'll see in <b>Scion: God</b> what it looks like from the other side; but I highly doubt it will be \u201cthey're an \u00c1os Sidhe! Darn; I can't Adopt them because I'm not Irish!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T21:26:46-07:00","id":1417511,"title":"","content":"I do not think Denizen Scions are limited in that way. As for what the consequences would be, I really hadn\u2019t thought it through. But that\u2019s definitely an interesting question. Imagine a cyclops who was adopted as a Scion of Thor...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T07:34:56-07:00","id":1417633,"title":"","content":"I think there's a sidebar in Origin noting that yes, there are converts and mingling cultures in the World, so you could be a Kitsune who's not that tied to Shintoism or Buddhism.<br /> <br /> And if you're a fox spirit who caught the eyes of Artemis, I doubt there's some kind of catch-all &quot;Nope you gotta stay in your box&quot; cosmic underlining that will stop Artemis from making you a Scion.<br /> <br /> 'Cause like, that's never been how things worked with religion. Stories spread. They mingle. Figures from different religions crossed boundaries all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","ava